APS-018 — Policy Audit

Document ID: APS-018
Title: Policy Audit
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Policy Audit Model (CPAM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Policy Audit Model establishes the principles, structures, processes, evidence requirements, and governance necessary to independently verify policy governance, evaluation, enforcement, compliance, exceptions, distribution, federation, and lifecycle activities.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Audit architecture
Audit planning
Audit execution
Audit evidence
Audit findings
Audit reporting
Audit governance
Continuous assurance

This specification applies to every governed policy activity within Atlas.

3. Canonical Definition

Policy Audit is the independent, evidence-based examination of Canonical Policy Objects and associated governance activities to determine conformity with applicable Atlas specifications, governance requirements, organizational obligations, and regulatory standards.

Policy Audit evaluates governance.

It SHALL NOT modify governance outcomes.

4. Objectives

The Policy Audit Model SHALL:

Verify governance integrity.
Verify policy compliance.
Preserve accountability.
Support certification.
Enable continuous assurance.
Preserve audit evidence.
Support independent review.
Enable reproducibility.
5. Audit Principles

Every audit SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Independence

Audit activities SHALL be performed independently of the audited activity.

Evidence-Based

Audit conclusions SHALL rely upon objective evidence.

Traceability

Every audit conclusion SHALL be traceable to supporting evidence.

Reproducibility

Equivalent audit evidence SHALL produce equivalent audit conclusions.

Explainability

Audit findings SHALL include sufficient rationale for independent review.

Integrity

Audit evidence SHALL remain immutable after collection.

