Audit SHALL remain independent of operational governance.

7. Auditable Activities

Atlas recognizes the following auditable policy activities.

Activity	Description
Policy Authoring	Creation and modification
Policy Approval	Governance approval
Policy Evaluation	Runtime evaluation
Policy Decision	Decision generation
Policy Enforcement	Directive execution
Policy Lifecycle	State transitions
Policy Compliance	Compliance assessments
Policy Exceptions	Exception management
Policy Distribution	Artifact deployment
Policy Federation	Cross-domain governance

Future specifications MAY introduce additional auditable activities.

8. Audit Planning

Every audit SHALL define:

Property	Description
Audit ID	Unique identifier
Audit Scope	Activities to be examined
Audit Objectives	Expected outcomes
Audit Criteria	Applicable requirements
Audit Authority	Responsible auditor
Audit Schedule	Planned execution
Audit Method	Manual, automated, or hybrid

Audit plans SHALL be governed Canonical Atlas Objects.

9. Audit Evidence

Every audit SHALL preserve evidence including:

Policy versions
Governance records
Evaluation records
Decision records
Exception records
Compliance reports
Distribution logs
Federation agreements
Digital signatures
Canonical Events

Evidence SHALL remain immutable and attributable.

10. Audit Findings

Atlas defines the following canonical finding categories.

Category	Description
Conformant	Requirement satisfied
Observation	Improvement opportunity
Minor Nonconformity	Limited deviation
Major Nonconformity	Significant deviation
Critical Nonconformity	Severe governance failure

Findings SHALL reference supporting evidence.

11. Corrective Actions

Every nonconformity SHALL define:

Action identifier
Related finding
Responsible authority
Required action
Due date
Completion criteria
Verification method

Corrective actions SHALL be independently governed.

12. Audit Lifecycle

Every audit SHALL progress through:

Planned
    │
Authorized
    │
Evidence Collected
    │
Evaluated
    │
Findings Issued
    │
Corrective Actions
    │
Verified
    │
Closed
    │
Archived

Lifecycle history SHALL remain immutable.

13. Continuous Assurance

Atlas SHALL support continuous audit through:

Automated evidence collection
Scheduled reassessment
Policy change monitoring
Compliance drift detection
Risk-triggered audits
Continuous reporting

Continuous assurance SHALL complement—not replace—formal audits.

14. Audit Governance

Every audit SHALL define:

Audit authority
Lead auditor
Independent reviewer
Applicable governance domain
Approval authority
Retention requirements

Audit governance SHALL remain independently auditable.

15. Audit Quality

Every audit SHALL satisfy:

Independence
Completeness
Objectivity
Repeatability
Traceability
Explainability
Timeliness
Auditability

Quality SHALL be continuously measured.

16. Audit Reporting

Every audit report SHALL include:

Audit scope
Criteria
Evidence summary
Findings
Risk assessment
Corrective actions
Overall conclusion
Recommendations

Reports SHALL be reproducible from the recorded evidence.

17. Conformance

A Policy Audit implementation conforms if it:

Implements canonical audit principles.
Preserves immutable evidence.
Supports independent evaluation.
Produces standardized findings.
Tracks corrective actions.
Maintains audit traceability.
Supports continuous assurance.
18. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted audit planning.
Autonomous evidence collection.
Predictive governance risk analysis.
Cross-federation audit coordination.
Formal audit proofs.
Continuous certification services.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical audit semantics.

